// dsc.bgm_swell — the water is getting worse
// Heard as "the same low woo as bgm_descent", which defeats the point: this
// layer exists to be crossfaded with bgm_descent, and two layers a listener
// cannot tell apart are worth one layer.
//
// What changed so the ear can sort them:
//   - the tritone is two octaves up and louder, so it sits above the root
//     instead of inside the same band
//   - the arc sweeps higher and wider, where bgm_descent's closes
//   - the low swell fires every two beats instead of every four
//   - saw() is already zero-mean, so nothing is subtracted from it here
bpm = 60

arc = sine(0.0625) * 400 + 1050
left_tones = saw(110) + saw(130.81) + saw(233.08) + saw(466.16) * 0.7
right_tones = saw(110.2) + saw(131.1) + saw(233.6) + saw(466.9) * 0.7
left_bed = left_tones * 0.075 |> lp(@, arc, 1.6)
right_bed = right_tones * 0.075 |> lp(@, arc, 1.6)
undertow = sine(55) * ar(trigger(2), 0.30, 0.5) * 0.10

out(stereo(left_bed, right_bed) + stereo(undertow, undertow) |> freeverb(@, 0.9, 0.6, 0.3, 0.45))
